# Epsilon parser helper slice using scoped names and bounded direct recursion.
# This ports ascii_between, is_digit, and decimal accumulation from the
# retained Epsilon compiler. Input replaces its immutable Bytes cursor so the
# call experiment remains within the state-machine slice's one-word ABI.

machine ascii_between 3 c word low word high word result word
state compare_low
brlt c low outside compare_high
state compare_high
brlt high c outside inside
state inside
const result 1
return result
state outside
const result 0
return result
end

machine is_digit 1 c word result word
local low word
local high word
state start
const low 48
const high 57
call result ascii_between 3 c low high
return result
end

machine epsilon_number_value 4 remaining word value word ten word ascii_zero word result word
local c word
local digit word
local next_remaining word
local next_value word
local one word
state next
brzero remaining done read_digit
state read_digit
read c
call digit is_digit 1 c
brzero digit invalid accumulate
state accumulate
const one 1
sub next_remaining remaining one
sub digit c ascii_zero
mul next_value value ten
add next_value next_value digit
call result epsilon_number_value 4 next_remaining next_value ten ascii_zero
return result
state invalid
const result 255
return result
state done
copy result value
return result
end

machine main 1 ignored word result word
local remaining word
local value word
local ten word
local ascii_zero word
state start
const remaining 3
const value 0
const ten 10
const ascii_zero 48
call result epsilon_number_value 4 remaining value ten ascii_zero
write result
halt ignored
end

entry main start